----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE — what shipped (parity with the web source)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web `WidgetBigNumber` is a PURE presentational widget primitive (a shared widget building block):
  it takes `value: number | null` plus optional `unit` / `label` / `subtitle` / `badge` / `valueColor`
  (default 'text-white') / `nullDisplay` (default '—') / `animated` (default true), and renders a centered
  column (web `flex flex-col items-center justify-center h-full gap-1`):
    • a baseline value row — the value as an `<AnimatedNumber>` count-up (animated) or a `tabular-nums`
      span (static), or the muted `nullDisplay` when `value === null`, with an optional `text-lg` unit affix
    • an optional uppercase `text-[10px]` tracking-wider label
    • an optional `text-xs` subtitle
    • an optional `<Badge>` (variant via badgeVariantMap: success/warning/error→danger/neutral)
  There is NO fetch / React-Query / Promise in the source, so it has NO loading/error/stale/offline branch
  (the host widget that owns the query renders those). Per the sibling presentational-primitive precedent
  (WidgetComparisonCard 0003, WidgetStatGrid 0010, Delta 0081, MetricCard 0095) this surface reproduces
  ONLY the source's REAL branches — inventing loading/error/stale/offline chrome would fabricate states the
  source does not have (Honesty Covenant #5, "no parity shortcuts" cuts both ways). The real branches:
    • value present, animated  (native AnimatedNumber 0075 — the faithful peer of web <AnimatedNumber/>)
    • value present, static    (monospaced display figure — the peer of web tabular-nums span)
    • value null  (the empty)  (muted nullDisplay figure — the source's own "no value" presentation,
                                the "never a blank box" leaf; web text-[var(--text-muted)])
  The count-up REUSES the shared native AnimatedNumber surface (0075); the badge chip is the verbatim-text
  peer of the shared TSBadge (web <Badge>), reusing its TSTone tokens (error→danger per badgeVariantMap).

  Files: WidgetBigNumber.Adapter/Model/.swift/Views/Previews/Tests/AdapterTests.swift + .strings (1221 LOC).
  Bindings : P1/S8 WidgetBigNumberModel @Observable holder (props + projection; no HTTP in the view);
             P1/S9 tokens (Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius/TSTypeMetrics) — no Tailwind ports, no hex;
             P1/S10 NSLocalizedString facade (table "WidgetBigNumber"); P1/S11 view.opened telemetry
             (slug "WidgetBigNumber", emitted once + idempotent across appear/disappear).
  i18n     : web source has 0 t() keys (anonymous; value/unit/label/subtitle/badge.text are caller-supplied,
             already-localized props rendered verbatim; nullDisplay defaults to the symbol "—"). The 2
             string entries are native a11y additions only: widgetBigNumber.valueUnit + .a11ySeparator. 0 dead.
  a11y     : the whole column folds into ONE VoiceOver element reading "{value}{unit}, {label}, {subtitle},
             {badge}" (skipping absent parts); the animated figure voices its settled value (not tween
             frames); Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce-Motion honored by the reused AnimatedNumber roller.
  valueColor: web className passthrough -> mapped to the theme-aware BigNumberValueTone token enum
             (primary[=white]/secondary/muted/success/danger/warning/accent), exactly as StatValueTone (0010).

